# Naming an empire goes through ES2Access/UI/EmpireNames.cs, which owns one method per form the game draws - leader name alone, faction symbol in front of it, leader-and-faction, and the coordination request's hand-built form.
# Calling GuiEmpire's namers directly, or reading an empire's Title or LocalizedName, picks a form by flag and is how a faction gets silently dropped and a fogged name silently leaked.
# Reading a label the game already composed is not one of these calls and needs no entry.
# Where a site truly cannot go through the helper, write `// name: <which drawn form this matches and why>` on the line above the call or at the end of it, then record the site here.
# An exception to this rule must be reported to the owner.
#
# Generated by ES2ACCESS_LINT_REGENERATE=empire-names; format: path | count | source line.
#
